WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.330
- One of the parts of growing up

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.870
is to getting your finances right.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.590
It's about taking control
of your own money,

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.630
of your own financial situations,

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.660
and making the right and
responsible decisions

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.740
for your life.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.090
Of course, this is easier said than done.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.800
Some of us have the
benefit to have the luxury

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.420
of coming from maybe parents

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.950
who taught us some of
these important principles

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.750
are those don't and those
need to learn these things

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.830
by themselves over
their 20s and their 30s.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.040
In this video, I wanted to share
some of the key principles,

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.560
some of the key thoughts
and considerations

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.290
that I personally picked up
during the course of my 20s,

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.760
and that for me, at least,

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.960
that is significant difference in my life,

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.350
and for my personal financial situation.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:47.090
One thing I wanna say in the
beginning is that these things,

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.280
these ideas that I will not
present were not invented by me.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.240
So these are things that
I picked up over time

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:55.360
by reading books, also
watching other YouTube videos.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.910
This is just the best off of these ideas

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.960
that I really made this for myself,

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.020
and I hope that this will
be helpful for you as well.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.910
So now without further
ado, let's get into it.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:06.660
So when it comes to another coffee break,

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.830
here on my channel Firm
Learning, my name is Heinrich,

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:12.080
and as you know, on my
channel, I want to help you

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.610
to be become successful in the
first years of your career.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.260
And for sure, getting your money right,

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:19.560
is a key part of that.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.330
So this is what we're
going to talk about today.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.930
And specifically I will
share five key lessons

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:25.710
that I picked up over time,

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:28.590
where I hope that these will
be helpful for you as well.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:31.510
The first principle that
I think is a very crucial

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:35.260
is the principle of paying yourself first.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:36.950
Because what do most people do wrong?

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.110
When most people get their paycheck,

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:42.310
there's already lots of taxes
deducted from the paycheck,

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.490
and then people spend the money

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.260
during the course of the month,

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.670
and then they think to themselves,

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:51.510
well, maybe at the end of the
month, if something is left,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:52.540
I will save it.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.373
I will invest it.

00:01:53.373 --> 00:01:54.260
I will take it aside.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.130
And then of course, no surplus
at the end of the month,

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.050
there often isn't much money left,

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:02.740
and then no, only very little
money is getting saved.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.510
And the idea of paying yourself
first is the following.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:08.380
So if you make a gross salary of 100%,

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:09.790
you're often in many countries,

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:12.010
depending of course, on the
exact income that you make,

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.450
and based on our tax system,

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:18.450
easily 40% of that salary
will be deducted by the state.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.360
You will need to pay in
taxes and so on and so forth.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.720
And clearly this would be the
deducted from your paycheck

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:24.860
in the very beginning.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:25.940
So this doesn't depend

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:27.640
on how much money you
have left or whatever.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.220
This is what will go out of your paycheck

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.280
from the very start.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.250
And then the logic is, well, if the IRS,

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.620
if the financial authorities

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.360
are taking this money away from you,

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.160
shouldn't you then make
sure that you pay yourself

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.530
that very same amount of money as well?

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.240
Shouldn't you make sure
that then roughly 40%

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.580
of your gross salary is taken aside,

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:50.010
is saved, is invested as well?

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.830
This at least makes a lot of sense to me.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:54.880
And if you assume that 40%
of the gross salary is taxes,

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.420
then 60% are your net salary.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.460
This would then mean that
one third of your net salary

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.340
is really only what you
have available for living,

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.700
which would correspond to a
savings rate of about 66%.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.370
This is of course quite significant.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.890
And I once made a video that
I will link some above here,

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:15.280
where I talked about having
a savings rate of 50%.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.460
And of course, it's also
clear that the more you earn,

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.410
the more privileged you
are with your salary,

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.030
the easier it will be for you

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.060
to save a substantial portion of that.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.590
But at least as an aspiration,

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.280
as a goal that you aspire
towards, having that in mind

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.130
that you should probably pay yourself,

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.780
invest at least as much money

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.860
as the state takes away from you.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:35.310
Related to that is the idea of not waiting

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.110
until the end of the month.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.850
Until you take the money aside,

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:40.430
and then put it in your savings account

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.320
or into your investments.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.510
But instead, make sure that you
take all this money directly

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:46.730
after your salary hits your bank account.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.800
And you can do this in
different ways, for instance,

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.630
with a regular savings plan

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.480
that automatically then deducts the money

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.260
and puts it into the savings account,

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.300
or with an automated stock investment plan

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.440
where it can do all that.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:00.130
But don't make it dependent
on your discipline,

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.800
but rather make sure that you invest it,

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.380
and then figure out how
to live on the rest.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.083
At least assuming that
you're privileged enough

00:04:06.083 --> 00:04:08.310
that this is (indistinct)
possible for you.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:10.280
The second idea that
I wanna share with you

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.070
that I've found insanely valuable

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:15.610
is the idea of never touch principal.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.180
So this is coming from finance,

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:19.130
where you distinguish
between the principal.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.140
So the capital invested, for instance,

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:24.320
the capital invested into a
bond, and then the interest.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.570
The interest that this capital pays.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.790
And the key idea is that over time

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.470
you will build your capital.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.710
You will build your
principal if you follow

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.410
especially also advice number one.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.700
Every month, you will put money aside,

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.170
invest it for instance,
into the stock market.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.720
This is the principal that
you will accrue over time,

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.290
and the principal that for
you will grow over time.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:47.780
And the key point here is
that you should make sure

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.100
that you organize your life

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.873
in a way that you should
really make it a rule

00:04:51.873 --> 00:04:54.960
that you do not take money out of that.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.220
Never ever take money out
of this principal account.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:01.030
Where you collect money, where
your capital is building.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.910
Instead, you should
aspire to the situation

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.940
that maybe at some point in the future,

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:06.580
you live just by the interest.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.190
So if your stocks pay dividends,

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:11.660
if your investments pay any
other type of interest, yes,

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.980
this is the money that
will available to you.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.610
This is the money that
potentially at some point

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:18.650
you might also be able to spend,

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.140
but I would encourage you to especially

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:22.030
in the beginning rather reinvest it.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:22.863
But at some point,

00:05:22.863 --> 00:05:24.540
if you really make this a habit of yours,

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.700
of saving the money,
of investing the money,

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.600
if you're lucky enough,
if this plays out well,

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:29.800
at some point in your life,

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:30.910
you will be in a situation

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.310
where maybe all of your regular expenses,

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.700
all of your daily expenses,

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:38.230
you will be able just to
pay out of the interest

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.020
of the capital that you have invested.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.860
This is also a variation of this idea

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.520
of passive income, right?

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.516
That you create income,

00:05:44.516 --> 00:05:46.980
which does not need to be earned anymore.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:50.100
That you're not dependent
anymore on your labor income,

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.920
but that you just can earn
income out of your principal.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.590
The third point I want
to share with you today

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:59.320
is that you should really
absolutely track your net worth.

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.440
There's one famous saying in consulting,

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.480
probably not only consulting,

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.730
but rather general management wisdom,

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:08.700
which is you cannot manage
what you do not measure.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:12.410
So if you do not measure your
net worth on a regular basis,

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:15.140
chances are higher that
you will really struggle

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.830
to manage that in the
way that it will regrow

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.990
to make sure that your
principal is growing over time.

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:23.090
And here, I also made a video in the past

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:25.150
where I talked about
how you can really track

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.930
this net worth, what the
net worth actually is,

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.030
how it is defined,

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:32.160
and even shared with you
a basic Excel spreadsheet,

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.860
where you really can do all this.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.270
I will link it somewhere above here.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:36.360
It's really the same tool,

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.800
the same Excel spreadsheet
that I use myself.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:40.900
So hope that this is detailed for, to you.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.680
And as you can just check out this video,

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.980
I will not repeat myself, but
just really wanna emphasize.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:47.120
So from my perspective,

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:51.180
this is just crucial for you
accumulating wealth over time.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.710
My insight number four

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:55.570
is that you just cannot start too early.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:58.810
And this is probably a
mistake that also I myself did

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.262
because in my early
20s, what I thought was,

00:07:01.262 --> 00:07:03.650
now I still don't earn that much money.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:05.750
I was still at university at the time.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.790
Why should I now really
restrict my lifestyle

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.610
if I don't have that much money, anyway?

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.130
What is really the value of saving

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.040
one or 200 Euro every month

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:17.330
if this really restricts my
lifestyle in a significant way?

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.210
And then probably later down the road,

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:20.710
it will be much easier for me

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.380
to save much more
significant amounts of money,

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.830
if I'm then like fully
arrived into the job market,

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:27.810
and then hopefully earn
some decent salaries.

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:29.300
This is what I was thinking at the time,

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.700
and I believe that this is
what many people are thinking.

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.630
What these people, and also I, myself

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:36.500
severely underestimated
at that point in time

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:39.100
is the power of compound interest.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.190
There are a lot of crazy,

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:42.240
really super counterintuitive,

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.810
mind blowing calculation examples.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.580
If you do some research on this
topic of compound interest,

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:48.413
but the bottom line

00:07:48.413 --> 00:07:50.630
is that it makes a significant difference.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.550
Whether you start investing in your 20s

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.790
compared to starting
investing in your 30s,

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:56.190
even though you just might start

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:59.378
with rather small amounts
of sums in your 20s.

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:02.800
You will very likely
significantly underestimate

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.870
the additional amount of money
that you will need to save

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.620
in your 30s, if you want to compensate

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:11.510
the money that you did
not save in your 20s,

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:15.010
even though these amounts
might've been only small amounts.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:18.060
Again, these calculation
examples are really eye opening.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.870
I included one of them in this video

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:22.420
where I talked about the 50% savings rate.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.300
I very much encourage
you to check this out

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:25.680
if you haven't seen it yet.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:29.530
My big recommendation to you
really is start investing

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:32.380
as early as possible, maybe
already in your high school,

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:33.620
just to get used of it.

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:34.453
For sure in university,

00:08:34.453 --> 00:08:37.280
even if it's only 100 Euro every month,

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.480
it will really make a
significant difference

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:40.850
over the long-term

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.860
if you do this in a
good and consistent way.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:45.260
Last but not least, my
insight number five,

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:49.030
and this is do things beyond
your nine-to-five job.

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:50.860
And this tip is especially important

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:52.550
for people maybe not working

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.700
in these super accelerated career tracks

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:57.980
that you have almost no
time of doing anything else

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:58.880
besides your job.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.390
But the truth is that most
people live or work in a job

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:04.330
that goes from nine to
five, as it says, right?

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:06.660
So usually at 5:00 PM or at 6:00 PM,

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:09.070
you come home and then
you have the free evening

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:11.260
until the next day you
move back into your job.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:13.720
And of course, it's great to
spend time with your family.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.680
Of course, it's also great to watch TV,

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.220
to maybe watch Netflix.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.890
And you're for sure just
up to every single one

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.930
to prioritize your time and
make these decisions for you.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:24.880
But especially, if you find yourself

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.305
sitting in front of the TV

00:09:26.305 --> 00:09:30.050
or sitting in front of the
computer every single evening,

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:32.090
not really doing the things

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.760
that will do the difference
for you in the longterm,

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.100
I would challenge yourself

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:37.990
whether you wouldn't find the time

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:40.170
to rather work on some side projects,

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.840
to work on a couple of ideas,

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:43.510
which they may be in the longterm

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:46.230
might create some additional
income for yourself

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.630
on top of your daily nine-to-five job.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:51.810
Because one thing is for sure,
while it might feel great

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:53.740
to watch Netflix in the evening,

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:56.450
and I'm for sure guilty
of that regularly as well,

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.740
you could have invested that time

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.720
in some productive activities
that really pay you

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:03.530
in the longterm in the evening.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:06.710
And for sure, I truly believe
that a significant portion

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.070
of where you will be
in five years from now,

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:12.160
in 10 years from now,
in 20 years from now,

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:16.120
will be determined how you
spend this additional time

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:17.050
in the evening.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.400
Spending this time in a productive way

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.640
can make the difference in your life,

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.230
can really have a huge
impact on your life,

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:25.410
on your career,

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:28.310
that is probably not even
possible to overestimate.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:31.100
So now I would love to hear
from you, does this resonate?

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.420
Does this makes sense?

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:33.440
What are your tips?

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.240
What are your insights that you collected

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:36.640
over the course of your life,

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:38.070
which maybe you would love to share

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.940
back to the Firm Learning community?

